               1oo% Wall V1.4 (c) by Neurodancer/ABYSS/100%
               --------------------------------------------

This  Wall  is meant for CNet 3.05+ only, I don't know if it works with the
older  versions  (2.63  and  so  on...).   This version is no longer Public
Domain,  yet  still  freely  distributable.   Anyone who's so bored to fuzz
around  so  lame in my cheap program:  I feel sorry for you.  Typically for
the  Amiga  scene  of today:  make a show out of nothing, talking bullshit,
    exaggerating everything and DOING NOTHING really worth to meantion.


                                Disclaimer
                                ----------
Please note that I won't take ANY resposibilty or guarantee if this program
crashes  your  machine, kills your dog, or does anything else (even working
                 normal) - use ENTIRELY at YOUR OWN RISK.


                                 Features
                                 --------
o Automagically =) adapts to the callers terminal height! No short walls
  with only 8 entries if caller has a big terminal screen!
o Configurable maximum storage capacity of the wall
o Filters MCI- & ESC-Codes from the users entry! No hacking!
o OK prompts for all important entries
o Optionally adds writers handle
o Maximum input length, checks length of the handle if to be added.
o Fantastic :) selfmade 8- & 16-color ANSIs included!
o Easy include of own Wall-ANSIs
o Auto-recognizes height of ANSI.
o Exits immediately if carrier lost

The  included ANSIs are for 8 color Amiga terminals (tt3), and for 16 color
IBM  gfx  font  terminals (tt4).  Actually, tt4 is the Amiga Skypix mode of
C-Net, but its the only mode besides Amiga Int'l that does no conversion of
the output.  If you only support one charset in your bbs, simply rename the
                         stuff as you like.  bla.


                               Installation
                               ------------
Move  the  whole  stuff to your PFiles:  directory.  If you have some other
1oo%  tools  (¹)  installed, its likely you already have a mother dir "1oo"
  there.  Place this program in "pfiles:1oo/wall/" and you're off to go.

Datafiles  from  previous "Acied Wall 1.3" can be used, although the output
has changed a bit (the input line length is now sensitive for the length of
                  the writers handle - if not anonymous).

Furthermore,  you  can  change  the first few values in the script that say
        "maxline" for the maximum of wall lines you want to store.


